RC390 Codebase Rules & Conventions
1. Package Management
Always use Yarn for installing, updating, and managing dependencies.
Example commands:
yarn install
yarn add <package>
yarn remove <package>
Do not use npm or other package managers.

2. Folder Structure
Project Root:
rc390/
│
├── api/                    # (Backend or API-related code, if any)
├── public/                 # Static public assets (served as-is)
│   └── assets/             # Audio, 3D models, PDFs, images
├── src/                    # All source code
│   ├── assets/             # Images, icons, and static assets for components
│   ├── components/         # (If present) Shared React components
│   ├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks
│   ├── layouts/            # Layout and provider components (Theme, ErrorBoundary, etc.)
│   ├── manual/             # (If present) Manual or documentation-related code
│   ├── modules/            # Feature-specific modules (e.g., 3D/Three.js logic)
│   ├── pages/              # Page-level React components (for routing)
│   ├── services/           # API calls and service logic
│   ├── theme/              # Theming, CSS variables, Tailwind config, and design system
│   │   ├── constants/      # CSS variable definitions
│   ├── ui/                 # Reusable UI components (Navbar, buttons, cards, etc.)
│   │   ├── audio/          # Audio-related UI components
│   │   └── controls/       # UI controls (e.g., camera sliders)
│   ├── utils/              # Utility/helper functions
│   ├── 3d/                 # 3D models, controls, and related files
│   ├── App.jsx             # Main App component
│   ├── main.jsx            # Entry point
│   └── index.css           # Global styles
│
├── package.json            # Project metadata and dependencies
├── yarn.lock               # Yarn lockfile (do not delete)
├── tailwind.config.js      # Tailwind CSS configuration
├── postcss.config.js       # PostCSS configuration
├── vite.config.js          # Vite build configuration
├── eslint.config.js        # ESLint configuration
├── README.md               # Project overview
└── index.html              # Main HTML file

3. Additional Structure & Usage Notes
All new dependencies must be added with Yarn.
Do not modify or delete yarn.lock.
Static assets (audio, 3D models, PDFs) go in public/assets/.
Component-specific assets go in src/assets/.
3D-related code is organized under src/3d/ and src/modules/.
Theming is managed via CSS variables in src/theme/constants/variables.css and Tailwind config.
Each major directory (hooks, layouts, modules, pages, services, theme, ui, utils) should have a README.md describing its purpose and usage.



1. Project Structure & Organization
Directory Structure:
src/pages/ - Page components for routing
src/ui/ - Reusable UI components
src/layouts/ - Layout components and providers
src/hooks/ - Custom React hooks
src/modules/ - Feature-specific modules
src/theme/ - Styling and theme files
src/assets/ - Static assets (images, icons)
src/utils/ - Utility functions
src/services/ - API and external services
src/3d/ - 3D models and Three.js related files
File Naming:
React components: PascalCase (e.g., Home.jsx, ThemeProvider.jsx)
Hooks: camelCase with use prefix (e.g., usephone.js, useTextScramble.js)
Utilities: camelCase (e.g., nav-items.jsx)
CSS files: kebab-case (e.g., bike-theme.css, nfs-navbar.css)
2. React Component Patterns
Component Structure:
import React from "react";
import { Helmet } from "react-helmet-async";
// External imports first, then internal imports

export default function ComponentName() {
  // Hooks at the top
  // Component logic
  
  return (
    <div className="relative flex flex-col items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-[var(--color-bg)]">
      <Helmet>
        <title>Page Title | MidnightTorque</title>
        <meta name="description" content="..." />
        <meta name="keywords" content="..." />
        <meta property="og:title" content="..." />
        <meta property="og:description" content="..." />
      </Helmet>
      {/* Component content */}
    </div>
  );
}
Import Order:
React and React-related imports
Third-party libraries
Internal components (UI, layouts, etc.)
Hooks
Assets and static files
Export Pattern:
Use export default for main component
Named exports for utilities and constants
3. Styling Conventions
CSS Variables System:
Use CSS custom properties defined in src/theme/constants/variables.css
Color palette: --color-primary, --color-surface, --color-accent, etc.
Typography: --font-hero, --font-h1, --font-body, etc.
Spacing: --spacing-xs, --spacing-sm, --spacing-md, etc.
Tailwind + CSS Variables:

Theme Structure:
Global styles in src/index.css
Component-specific styles in dedicated CSS files
Theme variables in src/theme/constants/variables.css
Responsive breakpoints defined in CSS variables
className="relative flex flex-col items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-[var(--color-bg)]"


4. State Management & Hooks
Custom Hooks Pattern:

Context Providers:
Wrap providers in src/main.jsx in this order:
HelmetProvider
ErrorBoundary
QueryProvider
ThemeProvider
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

export default function useCustomHook() {
  const [state, setState] = useState(initialValue);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Effect logic
    return () => {
      // Cleanup
    };
  }, []);

  return { state, setState };
}


5. Routing & Navigation
Routing Structure:
Use React Router DOM with BrowserRouter
Pages in src/pages/ directory
Navigation items defined in src/ui/nav-items.jsx
Navigation Items Pattern:
export const NAV_ITEMS = [
  {
    label: "Page Name",
    to: "/route",
    iconSmall: <svg>...</svg>,
    iconLarge: <svg>...</svg>,
  },
];


6. Error Handling
Error Boundary:
Class-based component in src/layouts/ErrorBoundary.jsx
Analytics integration with window.gtag
Graceful error display with styling
7. Performance & Optimization
Asset Management:
Static assets in public/assets/
Component assets in src/assets/
3D models in public/assets/ and src/3d/
Code Splitting:
Page-level components for route-based splitting
Lazy loading for heavy components
8. Accessibility & SEO
SEO Requirements:
Every page must have <Helmet> with:
Title format: "Page Name | MidnightTorque"
Meta description
Keywords
Open Graph properties
Accessibility:
Use semantic HTML elements
Include aria-hidden="true" for decorative elements
Proper alt text for images
9. Development Standards
ESLint Configuration:
Use ES2020+ features
React Hooks rules enforced
Custom rule: 'no-unused-vars': ['error', { varsIgnorePattern: '^[A-Z_]' }]
File Extensions:
React components: .jsx
JavaScript utilities: .js
Stylesheets: .css
10. Build & Deployment
Vite Configuration:
React plugin enabled
ES modules ("type": "module" in package.json)
Dependencies:
React 19.1.0+
Three.js and React Three Fiber for 3D
Tailwind CSS for styling
React Router DOM for routing
GSAP for animations
11. Naming Conventions
Variables & Functions:
camelCase for variables and functions
PascalCase for React components
UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants
CSS Classes:
Use Tailwind utility classes
Custom CSS classes in kebab-case
CSS variables with -- prefix
12. Code Organization Best Practices
Keep components focused and single-responsibility
Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
Use CSS variables for consistent theming
Maintain clean import organization
Include comprehensive README files in each directory
Use TypeScript-style JSDoc comments where helpful
These rules ensure consistency with the existing KTM RC390 codebase structure, maintaining the motorcycle/racing theme, modern React patterns, and performance-focused architecture.